# TT.TICKET_INTERFACE -- the simple attribute writers: change_customer_reference
# (S-TICKET-015/018), change_partner_reference (S-TICKET-022), change_label in BOTH
# overloads (2-arg S-TICKET-019, 3/4-arg S-TICKET-020), change_always_visible
# (S-TICKET-026), change_notification (S-TICKET-027) and change_summary (S-TICKET-028/029).
# Every step records 'ok' or the error code; probes compare the ticket rows and the audit
# events written (type, visibility, texts) -- never event ids (sequence-generated).
#
# Deliberately includes the Pitfall-2 inputs the spec's Checklist dimension 1 discusses:
# an empty string '' for customer_reference (step 03), for change_notification's public
# text (step 17) and for both change_summary texts (step 22). Oracle collapses '' to NULL
# for VARCHAR2 arguments; PostgreSQL does not -- any difference here is a finding, not an
# artifact (the normaliser only collapses ''/NULL in the OUTPUT columns, R3).
#
# Steps 14 and 17b pass a p_zitadel_contact_id to change_always_visible: Oracle's call to
# the private add_status_change_event has only 5 positional args (the zitadel id lands in
# p_private_change_text, S-TICKET-025/026 header note of the translation) -- reproduced,
# so both sides must show details_private = the id.
#
# known.diff: S-TICKET-059 (CORRECTION of the add_status_change_event cust_id bug,
# S-TICKET-053), two visible consequences, both frozen from the live run of 2026-10-21:
#   (i)  Oracle writes company_id = NULL on every audit event produced through
#        add_status_change_event (10 events on ticket A, 4 on ticket B; the 3 change_label
#        events carry a company on both sides); the translation resolves the ticket's
#        company, so PostgreSQL shows 13 / 4 'set'. The last probe isolates exactly that
#        (events grouped by company_id null/set); the other probes do not select it.
#   (ii) step 23, change_customer_reference on a nonexistent ticket: Oracle succeeds
#        (the UPDATE touches no row, the orphan tt.event row is inserted because the
#        harness runs with SET CONSTRAINTS ALL DEFERRED and never commits, so the FK
#        ORA-02291 the clause mentions never fires); the translation's company lookup
#        raises NO_DATA_FOUND (P0002) before anything is written -- exactly the "only the
#        error identity changes" part of S-TICKET-059.
# Steps 17 and 22 were DIFF on the first live run (2026-10-21) and are PASS since the
# S-TICKET-027/029 amendment + translation fix (NULLIF boundary normalisation).
#
# ORA_USER=system: the fixtures insert into stop.company, stop.contact, mss.host,
# mss.service and mss.host2service; TT holds only SELECT on those. Rolled back at the end.
ORA_USER=system
COMMITS=no
COMPARE_MSG=no
DESCRIPTION=change_customer_reference, change_partner_reference, change_label (2- and 4-arg), change_always_visible, change_notification, change_summary on tickets 952010/952011 incl. empty-string inputs
